# Default-deny: only files explicitly COPY'd in the Dockerfile end up in
# the image. Without this file the entire build context (including
# `.env`, `.git`, the local `.venv`, test fixtures, IDE state, caches,
# and build artifacts) gets baked into the published layer.
#
# Security review (2026-04-30) confirmed `/app/.env` had been embedded
# in built images, exposing OPENBRIDGE_REFRESH_TOKEN values. This file
# closes that hole.
*

# Source we DO want — every entry below must match the COPY lines in
# the Dockerfile or it will be invisible to the build.
!main.py
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!src/
!schemas/
# FastMCP SkillsDirectoryProvider reads ./skills/<skill>/SKILL.md and
# supporting files (references/*.md, evals/*) at runtime. Whitelist
# them so `COPY skills/ /app/skills/` finds them in the build context.
!skills/

# Re-deny anything that snuck into the allow-listed dirs above.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
# macOS AppleDouble resource-fork sidecar files. `tar` on darwin
# emits these alongside every regular file when packaging a directory
# with extended attributes; FastMCP's SkillsDirectoryProvider would
# otherwise expose them as supporting resources (e.g.
# skill://openbridge-mcp/._SKILL.md). Verified 2026-05-01.
**/._*
**/.DS_Store
